      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's just exhausting. all this talk about \"resilience\" and \"inspiring others\" feels so hollow when you're actually living in the wreckage. i'm just tired of fighting a battle that was lost before it even started. it feels like there's no real way to move forward when the damage is this permanent. everything i worked for is gone, and the people I thought I could trust are gone too. it's like the world has already moved on and decided i don't matter. sometimes i look at everything and i just think... maybe the only real way to win is to just stop playing the game entirely. to just stop fighting and let it go. do you ever think that maybe some things are just too broken to fix?",
